Original commit body from 0659ba2:

Extends parameter type inference (already in Python) to three more
language analyzers. Method calls on typed parameters now resolve:

- Java: void process(Client c) { c.send(); } → Client.send
- Kotlin: fun handle(db: Database) { db.save() } → Database.save
- TypeScript: function run(svc: Service) { svc.call() } → Service.call

Previously type inference only worked for constructor-assigned variables.
This improves call graph completeness for dependency injection patterns
(Spring, Dagger, FastAPI deps, etc.).

Each analyzer now extracts parameter types from function/method
declarations and adds them to the var_types dict used for method
call resolution.
